    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let the roots of the polynomial be $r,$ $s,$ and $t.$\n\nThen by Vieta's Formulas ($a,$ $b,$ $c$ denoting the coefficients of the polynomial):\n\n$-3 = r + s + t.$\n\n$1 = rs + rt + st.$\n\n$a = -3(r + s + t) = -6.$\n\nThe only possible value of $a$ such that $\\{ r,s,t \\} \\subset \\mathbb{Z}$ is $\\boxed{-6}.$. The answer is -6",
